# romdev memory-region exposure for the blueMSX (MSX / MSX2) libretro core.
#
# blueMSX keeps its V9938 VDP state in a file-static `struct VDP` (singleton
# `theVdp` in VDP.c) with no public accessors, so this patch adds five tiny
# getters in VDP.c (+ decls in VDP.h) returning live pointers into theVdp, then
# wires region cases in libretro.c. The Z80/R800 CPU is reachable from libretro.c
# via the already-present `extern BoardInfo boardInfo` / `(R800*)boardInfo.cpuRef`
# (the core uses that exact cast elsewhere); its active register bank `regs` is
# snapshotted into a flat little-endian buffer.
#
# Region IDs (romdev 0x1C0 block, must match src/host/types.js):
#   MSX_VRAM       0x1C0   UInt8[VRAM_SIZE=192KB]  V9938 VRAM (size reported = live vramSize)
#   MSX_VDP_REGS   0x1C1   UInt8[64]               VDP register file
#   MSX_VDP_STATUS 0x1C2   UInt8[16]               VDP status registers
#   MSX_PALETTE    0x1C3   UInt16[16]   = 32 B     paletteReg (9-bit GRB)
#   MSX_CPU_REGS   0x1C4   snapshot                AF/BC/DE/HL/IX/IY/PC/SP + I/R/iff/im/halt
#   MSX_PSG_REGS   0x1C5   UInt8[16]               AY-3-8910 register file (via a singleton
#                                                  captured in ay8910Create + a getter in AY8910.c)
#
# Execution breakpoints (runUntilPC / runUntilRead / stepInstruction):
#   Adds Z80/R800 hooks in Src/Z80/R800.c — a PC-break/single-step check at the
#   top of the r800Execute / r800ExecuteUntil run loops (PC compared BEFORE the
#   next opcode fetch; on hit it freezes the CPU at that PC and sets
#   r800->terminate so the active run loop returns and retro_run completes the
#   frame), plus READ and WRITE watchpoint hooks in readMem/writeMem (data path,
#   not opcode fetch). libretro.c exports the romdev_pcbreak_*/romdev_readwatch_*/
#   romdev_watchpoint_* setters+getters (same [out5]/[out6] layout as the gpgx
#   m68k template). romdev_pc_step is a per-instruction countdown the host arms to
#   2 so single-step ADVANCES the PC.
#
# Instruction WATCHDOG (callSubroutine can't hang anymore):
#   A standalone-driven routine (e.g. a decompressor fed a wrong arg) can loop
#   FOREVER inside one r800Execute / retro_run frame, so the host's per-FRAME cap
#   never runs and the whole WASM hangs. ROMDEV_WATCHDOG_CHECK (in Src/Z80/R800.c,
#   FIRST in BOTH run loops, before the PC-break check) counts dispatched
#   instructions and force-stops at romdev_pc_wd_limit — sets romdev_pc_hit +
#   romdev_pc_watchdog and ends the frame the SAME way the PC-break does
#   (terminate=1; break). libretro.c exports romdev_watchdog_set(limit) (the host
#   arms it before callSubroutine; 0 = off) and pcbreak_get now reports the
#   watchdog-tripped flag in out6[5]. Build script adds _romdev_watchdog_set to
#   EXPORTED_FUNCTIONS via WD_EXPORTS.
#
# RE primitives round 2 (register read/write + range-watch + PC-coverage):
#   Adds the cross-core RE round-2 exports to the Z80/R800 path. romdev_setreg/
#   romdev_getreg map the STABLE Z80 reg-id convention (0=A 1=F 2=B 3=C 4=D 5=E
#   6=H 7=L 8=IX 9=IY 16=PC 18=SP) onto the R800 active register bank
#   (cpu->regs, via boardInfo.cpuRef) — drives callSubroutine/setRegister.
#   romdev_range_set/get logs EVERY {pc,addr,value} touching [lo,hi] (readMem/
#   writeMem data hooks, mode 1=read 2=write 3=both) for watchRange; romdev_cov_
#   set/get records DISTINCT in-window PCs (a coverage check at the top of the
#   r800Execute/r800ExecuteUntil loops, beside the PC-break check) for logPCRange.
#   State lives in Src/Z80/R800.c; the six exports in libretro.c. Build script
#   adds them to EXPORTED_FUNCTIONS via RE2_EXPORTS.
#
